{{! allcrud-generator override of openapi-generator's embedded JavaSpring/apiController.mustache.
    Drops the stock delegate pattern entirely: the generated class extends CrudController
    directly, inheriting every REST mapping from the Allcrud base class, so this file only
    needs to implement the getService()/getConverter() hooks.

    allcrudEntityName / allcrudPojoClassName / allcrudIdType are resolved by
    AllcrudSpringCodegen#postProcessOperationsWithModels (a custom CodegenConfig, not the
    stock "spring" one) by inspecting the actual OpenAPI model - not hardcoded here anymore.
    allcrudEntityName (entity) is still assumed to be hand-written by the consuming project
    - this generator does not produce entities. The entity package path
    (org.openapitools.entity) is a placeholder, provisional until configurable package
    mapping is implemented - do not read it as an intentional final convention.
    The generated "Service" and "Converter" classes (see service.mustache,
    converter.mustache) are siblings in this same package, so no import is needed for
    either of them.
    Generated class name is prefixed with allcrudEntityName ("Product"), not the stock
    per-tag classname variable ("ProductsApi" - derived from the OpenAPI tag, plural, with
    an "Api" suffix SpringCodegen adds by convention) - that mismatch was a naming bug
    fixed after the fact, not an intentional customization. }}
